<article class="env-lemma" id="03GZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03GZ">Lemma <span data-tag="03GZ">37.53.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $s \in S$. Then $X_ s$ is geometrically connected, if and only if for every étale neighbourhood $(U, u) \to (S, s)$ the base change $X_ U \to U$ has connected fibre $X_ u$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $X_ s$ is geometrically connected, then any base change of it is connected. On the other hand, suppose that $X_ s$ is not geometrically connected. Then by Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0389" data-tag="0389">33.7.11</a> we see that $X_ s \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (s))} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ is disconnected for some finite separable field extension $k/\kappa (s)$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02LF" data-tag="02LF">37.35.2</a> there exists an affine étale neighbourhood $(U, u) \to (S, s)$ such that $\kappa (u)/\kappa (s)$ is identified with $k/\kappa (s)$. In this case $X_ u$ is disconnected. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>